  ],
  "steps": [
    "Invoke the native roadmap provider on the supplied model and source variants.",
    "Compare explicit expected facts, source bindings, native refusals and original project bytes/modes; compare isolated Core and PYZ observations.",
    "Exercise date/error boundaries and explicit dependency cycles without recomputation, mutation or live-source substitution; enforce process/network/write traps in isolated Core/PYZ.",
    "13.h.W: resolve Roadmap facts and optional native eight-gate Readiness through built-in views; compare exact direct-provider data, gate/selection hashes and unavailable/provisional/blocked states. Verify Coverage/Traceability selection parity and input admission through read-only render adapters, without inspecting rendered output.",
    "13.h.R: retain full native Built-in and Readiness semantic Work input, recompute with the original snapshot and fresh native services, and compare direct coverage/query, view and resumed projection. Persist complete source inputs in native Work storage; restore in isolated Core/PYZ while preserving pending work. Reject changed model, evaluation, time, product binding and absent required review authentication.",
    "13.h.C: rerun unchanged W/R and affected regression behavior after extracting common native calculated providers and shared view/readiness admission. Preserve public errors, validation order, snapshots, exact data/hashes, eight gates, pending Work and allowed effects. Renderer output is not an oracle."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Die Roadmap-Ansicht MUSS ausschließlich aus Artefakten, Beziehungen, Prioritäten, Risiken und Terminen des kanonischen Modells abgeleitet werden.",
    "scope": "Native roadmap projection derives explicit planning, priority, risk, date and dependency facts solely from supplied artifact bytes and original edges; binds exact origins and model root. R: calendar and schema errors preserve exact sources and file modes; dependency cycles and passive extension estimates never retime, estimate or publish data. Bound-input changes refuse output; foreign live changes remain intact and unverified. All existing W facts remain required. 13.h.W now integrates the available native Roadmap provider and optional bound native Readiness, plus Verification/Traceability selection parity. Unavailable calculations are not fabricated; rendering is never a pass oracle. 13.h.R additionally checks semantic Work-input resumption, exact data parity, no inherited gate pass, and unchanged pending native Work manifests. It does not claim a completed scheduler, public CLI or granular within-provider execution. 13.h.C only consolidates the existing native provider and input-binding implementation; no new semantic result, approval, completed Work unit or CLI contract."
  },
